}],"role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Extensions"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/Tree":{"title":"Tree","url":"\/documentation\/trees\/tree","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A tree: a connected, acyclic undirected graph with at least one vertex, so it has exactly","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"n − 1 edges, no self-loop and no parallel edges. The invariant is the type: every initializer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from unchecked input is failable, and a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tree"},{"text":" cannot be mutated.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Tree"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Tree"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Tree"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/Trees-Tree-Extensions":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Extensions to Tree","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/trees-tree-extensions","abstract":[{"text":"Members other modules add to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Tree"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Trees-Tree-Extensions"},"doc://ShortestPaths/documentation/ShortestPaths/Trees/Forest/init(_:)":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"init(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/trees\/forest\/init(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The shortest-path forest of a search from any number of sources, with the edges’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"directions and the roots dropped: every reached vertex, in the tree’s index order as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" lists them (unreached ones left out), and one edge (parent, child) per"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reached vertex with a parent, in that order. Edge positions are the forest’s own: edge k"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"joins the k-th listed vertex with a parent to its parent; the graph’s edge stays"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tree.parentEdge(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":". O(n); the vertices are hashed once, into the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"forest’s lookup table, unless they are the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":"s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<k"},{"type":"text","text":" in order."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Distance"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ShortestPathTree","preciseIdentifier":"s:13ShortestPaths0A8PathTreeV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Distance"},{"kind":"text","text":">)"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/Trees\/Forest\/init(_:)"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/Forest":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"Forest","url":"\/documentation\/trees\/forest","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Forest"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A forest: an acyclic undirected graph, possibly empty, so a disjoint union of trees (an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"isolated vertex is a one-vertex tree). ","type":"text"},{"code":"trees","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists them by least vertex, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"component(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" says which one a vertex is in.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Forest","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"stru